            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\n'mini.files' has its own way of \"move to trash\" instead of \"permanent delete\". Set `config.options.permanent_delete = false` and it will move files to a special directory (not trash). See [here](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/ddb435633319d06a466c74833ef340839b931bfe/doc/mini-files.txt#L593-L597) for more details.\r\n\r\nThe reasoning for not supporting trash is outlined in #390. Basically: too complex to do it right and cross-platform.",
